{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTATION LANDED FOR REVIEW — two stacked Gerrit changes, plus the live-tier status.\n\n * change 1097 'b4e3: make the DC backend reachable + conformant' — LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1.\n * change 1099 'b4e3: mint DC inbound identities as jira family' — pushed, awaiting votes.\n\nNOT submitting 1097 alone despite it being green. It widens reconciler.backend so a DC deployment\nbecomes configurable; landing that WITHOUT 1099 would ship exactly the silently-degraded DC inbound\nidentity path 1099 fixes. The stack submits together.\n\nEVIDENCE for the non-live ACs (all verified in this worktree, not asserted):\n * 1636 tests pass in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler; full tests/unit run 6159 passed / 19 skipped.\n * make lint = 0, make typecheck = 0 (mypy, 398 source files), module-size gate clean (no file > 800).\n * The contract-suite RED was precisely targeted: adding jira-datacenter to the fixture produced\n   EXACTLY ONE failure (test_isinstance_backend_facade) with 16 assertions passing — isolating the\n   defect to the two absent Protocol members rather than a broad breakage.\n * AC4 wording note, flagged rather than glossed: the criterion says the diff to\n   test_backend_contract.py is 'params-only'. It is not literally params-only — adding a third\n   backend needs an import and a construction branch (6 insertions, 3 deletions, all inside the\n   import block and the fixture). What the criterion is FOR does hold and is checkable: not one line\n   inside any 'def test_*' changed, so no assertion was weakened.\n\nLIVE TIER IS UNAVAILABLE IN THIS ENVIRONMENT — the operator-attested ACs are NOT met.\nI brought the J5 harness up rather than assert those ACs on faith. It did not merely boot slowly; it\nFAILED:\n\n  [ERROR] Failed to execute goal com.atlassian.maven.plugins:jira-maven-plugin:8.0.2:run ...\n  Cannot start container [Tomcat8xInstalledLocalContainer]: Deployable\n  [http://localhost:2990/cargocpc/index.html] failed to finish deploying within the timeout period\n  [2700000]. The Deployable state is thus unknown.\n\n45 minutes, then a hard timeout, on a host running several other containers. That is a resource/\nenvironment limitation, not a defect in this story's code. The live module\n(tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_reconcile_pass.py) is written, collects cleanly (3 tests), and its\nguards behave correctly with the harness absent — it SKIPS, and would FAIL LOUDLY if the harness were\nup with the [jira-datacenter] extra missing (that extra IS installed here, 3.10.5).\n\nSo these remain OPEN and need an operator with a working harness:\n  - the full reconcile pass converges and a repeated pass writes nothing (idempotence)\n  - the DC-created ticket provenance assertion\n  - the zero-unhandled-exceptions subprocess assertion\n\nI will not mark them met, and will not close this ticket on their behalf."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785471090305793001,"uuid":"2f58c85d-4dfe-4857-94ad-2f0f7772f8cb"}